    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23WZoZQWW6FN2CGdpXxqKa8)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Base: `main`; no dependency on open PRs.\n- Touches `sp-litnotes-meta.el`, its literate doc and its test file only.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-jm3f2q`, not number-prefixed: a cloud session cannot rename a branch after the PR number is known.\n\n## What it does\n\n- The `bib-project` picker (`sp-litnotes-meta--read-project`) now has `(none)` as a candidate.\n  - Choosing `(none)`, or an empty answer, adds no `bib-project` line.\n  - The thesis stays the default, so pressing RET behaves as before.\n- Same as `relevance-factor` and `read-priority`: nothing is remembered, so a later run asks again for a note that still lacks the line.\n- Unchanged:\n  - A note that already has `bib-project` is not asked.\n  - Batch commands (`preset`, `fill-all-*`, `backfill-children`) behave as before; \"no\" to the \"same project?\" question already skipped it, and the picker now also offers `(none)`.\n- `bib-project` is not read from BibTeX (only the picker, or the preset copied from a parent note), so no BibTeX value can lose to the prompt; existing values are never overwritten.\n- Literate doc updated as bullets (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org`); the `.el` matches the doc. No CHANGELOG edit; `when-let*` only.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`: 69 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3, including the new `sp-litnotes-meta-read-project-none-skips` (`(none)`, empty answer, and the default).\n\n## Not tested\n\n- The real minibuffer (Vertico ordering of `(none)`, prompt text) and the real vault.\n- `fill-all-convert` in a GUI session with `(none)` at the project question.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill` on a note without `bib-project`: the picker lists `(none)`; choose it, no `bib-project` line is added, other lines are filled\n- [ ] Same note again: the picker is asked again (nothing remembered); pressing RET picks the thesis\n- [ ] A note that already has `bib-project`: no question\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun`, then `-convert`: answer \"y\" to the project question, then `(none)`: no note gets `bib-project`\n- [ ] `sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children` from a note with `bib-project`: new notes copy it; from a note without one: none is asked or added\n- [ ] `relevance-factor` and `read-priority` prompts still work as before\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBbnQvkoywsh4PGEXV)_",
